  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="262d2f52-e31f-47b2-b66a-60f84a626b00"><problem><para>
      <para>A quadratic function \(f\) is defined by \(f(x)=(x-7)(x+3)\).</para>
      <para> Without graphing, identify the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph of \(f\).</para>
        </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((7,0),(-3,0)\)</para><para>\((-7,0),(3,0)\)</para><para>\((0,7),(0,-3)\)</para><para>\((0,-7),(0,3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\((7,0),(-3,0)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \((7,0)\0 and \((-3,0)\). If \(x\) is 7, \((7-7)(7+3)\) gives 0 10, which is 0. If \(x\) is -3, \((-3-7)(-3+3)\) gives -10 0, which is 0. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
